 "_freightNote": "The Baltic indices are a licensed product with no free feed. These are ETFs holding freight futures - they move with rates rather than with shipping equities, but carry roll cost and tracking error and can diverge from spot.",
 "_shareClassNote": "Ratio of the A price to the B price, with how far today sits from its own one-year mean. Pairs marked drifting have no stable mean to revert to - their level has moved over the year, so the standard-deviation figure describes the drift rather than an opportunity. This is an observation, not a recommendation: a spread can stay unusual for months, and whether switching is worth anything depends on tax, holding period and whether the votes matter to you."
